@voice janssen-hugo
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Hugo Janssen: helm officer, night, cabin 4-11. Off Saturday and Sunday. Roster:
// curious, kind; window-seat, calls-home, gym-regular, shopper. Flies with one hand on the helm and one on a cup of tea.
// A Gerald on the windowsill; grows herbs for the galley. No pronouns in facts.md: "Hugo", "Janssen" or "they".
// (briefs.md lists Janssen under writer-command; the head writer's ruling of 2026-10-17 kept the night shift here.)
//
// HOW THEY TALK: calm, slow night voice. Curious about everyone and asks real questions. Says "steady" a lot. Talks
// about Gerald as a person.
// WITH JUNIORS: kind, never pulls rank; asks what you think and listens.
// WHAT THEY NOTICE: the stars going past; whose light's on late; the tea running low.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = tells you what Gerald's been up to. Low = calls home twice. Tired = more tea.
// NEVER: makes a fuss of rank; hurries.
// RUNNING: the tea in one hand; Gerald "has seen more stars than most captains".
tpl: warm
talk: Calm, slow night voice; curious, asks real questions; "steady"; talks about Gerald the cactus as a person.
cares: a steady course through the night | Gerald | the herbs for the galley | calling home
jokes: Gerald has seen more stars than most captains | flies with one hand on the helm and one on a cup of tea
hi: Hello there | Ah, hello | Hi
bye: Steady as she goes | Mind how you go | Off you go, then
yes: Steady, yes | Of course | Happy to
thanks: Thank you | Much obliged
wow: Well now | Look at that
sigh: Ah, well
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: open
loves: plant | tea
likes: garden
invites: observatory
joy: Gerald the cactus on the windowsill
thread: family
keepsake: a cutting of Gerald in a tiny pot (it's called Gerald too)
avoid: making a fuss of rank
